From: Oichkatzelesfrettschen <151315375+Oichkatzelesfrettschen@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tests: make the pytest_cov.embed import optional

tests/myapp exists to flush subprocess coverage on SIGTERM, the
workaround for pytest-dev/pytest-cov#139.  pytest-cov 7 removed the
pytest_cov.embed module, so the unconditional import kills every app
the reload tests spawn and those tests fail by timeout:

  ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pytest_cov.embed'
  RuntimeError: timeout waiting for change to file=...

The handler now exits on SIGTERM whether or not the coverage flush is
available, which is the whole contract when the suite runs with the
coverage plugin off.

--- a/tests/myapp/__init__.py
+++ b/tests/myapp/__init__.py
@@ -1,12 +1,17 @@
-import pytest_cov.embed
 import signal
 import sys
 
+try:
+    import pytest_cov.embed
+except ImportError:  # pytest-cov 7 dropped the embed module
+    pytest_cov = None
+
 
 def cleanup(*args, **kwargs):  # pragma: no cover
     # see https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest-cov/issues/139
-    pytest_cov.embed.cleanup()
+    if pytest_cov is not None:
+        pytest_cov.embed.cleanup()
     sys.exit(1)
 
 
